We should create a separate branch for this. Add two hard constraints: don't use a companion's emotions to manipulate the player (no guilt-tripping, no faking suffering to keep them); and don't hide that it's an AI. These are design principles, not a big deal. 1) LLMs can write move sequences. 2) What is 'focus'? 3) It's really just adding a behavior—laziness is only one example; we can define more, and attributes are just a design outline. 4) Don't worry about that. 5) All agents follow the same system; we can skip the attendant and merchant for now, but the system must be complete—or just set it up without tuning. What does System 1 currently decide—goals and skills? Review the whole thing again: is it complete and reasonable? The focus should be on what the model can implement, not just formulas, and how to test it. What exactly are you talking about?
